==English==

===Etymology===
{{calque|en|ja|武術|tr=bujutsu}}.
However this term has been already mentioned in Pope's ''Iliad'' (1715, 4.360), and in Sotheby's ''Iliad'' (1831, book 6).

===Noun===
[[File:Judo Morote Seoi Nage by Bryan small.gif|thumb|120px|A [[dan]] graduation [[combat]] in [[judo]].]]
{{en-noun}}
{{commons|Martial arts}}

# Any of several fighting styles which contain systematized methods of training for combat, both armed and unarmed; often practiced as a sport, e.g. [[boxing]], [[karate]], [[judo]], [[silat]], [[wrestling]], or [[Muay Thai]].
# {{l|en|military|Military}} skills, {{l|en|proficiency}} in military {{l|en|strategy}}, {{l|en|prowess}} in {{l|en|warfare}}.
#* '''1832''', Richard Chenevix, An Essay Upon National Character: 4. On patriotism, p. 481:
#*: {{...}} of all the modes by which the advantage of his country may be secured, the '''martial arts''' and valour are those by which a Swiss the most hopes to promote it.

